    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0915" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary, War Department
                        General Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCarthy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Casablanca</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-18">January 18, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for: Mr.
                    Hopkins</hi>.</p>
                <p>We received the following message last night from General Eisenhower: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Yesterday Commander Butcher was told by Mr. Hopkins that the President
                            probably would Wish to see the war correspondents before he departs. As
                            virtually all correspondents in this theatre headquarter at Algiers, it
                            would be necessary to fly them to Casablanca. Suggest 15 representative
                            U.S. and British correspondents to be chosen by General McClure.
                            (General McClure handles public relations for General Eisenhower).
                            Please advise whether correspondents desired. If so, when and whether
                            the number is satisfactory.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Will you let me know what the President’s wishes in this matter are so that I may
                    inform General Eisenhower?<anchor n="1" xml:id="d445-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank McCarthy</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lt. Col., G.S.C. </hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d445-f1" n="1" xml:id="d445-f1-content">
                <p>About 50 correspondents were brought to Casablanca to attend the joint press
                    conference by Roosevelt and Churchill on January 24; for the record of that
                    conference, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg726">p.
                        726</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
